WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.188
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:09.013
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.313 --> 00:00:15.727
Unit four: Relative Clauses. Today you will give more information about people, things and places.

4
00:00:16.027 --> 00:00:18.761
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.910
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.507
Who.

7
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:27.017
Who means used for people.

8
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:29.407
The man who called is my uncle.

9
00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:32.715
Your turn. Say: Who.

10
00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:36.347
Who.

11
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:37.852
Which.

12
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.559
Which means used for things.

13
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:42.883
The book which I read is long.

14
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:45.915
Your turn. Say: Which.

15
00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:49.663
Which.

16
00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.162
That.

17
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.242
That means used for people or things.

18
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.524
The car that I bought is red.

19
00:00:57.117 --> 00:00:59.247
Your turn. Say: That.

20
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:02.950
That.

21
00:01:03.717 --> 00:01:04.544
Where.

22
00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.399
Where means used for places.

23
00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:09.971
This is the city where I was born.

24
00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:12.736
Your turn. Say: Where.

25
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.346
Where.

26
00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:17.945
Whose.

27
00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.601
Whose means shows possession.

28
00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:23.297
The boy whose bag is blue is Tom.

29
00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.420
Your turn. Say: Whose.

30
00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:30.140
Whose.

31
00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:32.349
Defining clause.

32
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:37.033
Defining clause means a clause that identifies exactly which one.

33
00:01:37.617 --> 00:01:39.651
A defining clause is essential.

34
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.413
Your turn. Say: Defining clause.

35
00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:47.709
Defining clause.

36
00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.939
Extra information.

37
00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.145
Extra information means details that are not essential.

38
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.342
Extra information is between commas.

39
00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.695
Your turn. Say: Extra information.

40
00:02:03.533 --> 00:02:05.022
Extra information.

41
00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:06.715
Connect.

42
00:02:07.717 --> 00:02:10.366
Connect means to join two ideas together.

43
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.170
Relative pronouns connect clauses.

44
00:02:13.783 --> 00:02:16.180
Your turn. Say: Connect.

45
00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:19.883
Connect.

46
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.061
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.917 --> 00:02:27.532
Visal, describe a person you know using who.

48
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:39.326
My teacher is a person who always helps me. A relative clause gives more information about a noun and connects two ideas without a new sentence.

49
00:02:40.417 --> 00:02:42.915
Which relative word do we choose?

50
00:02:44.017 --> 00:02:57.269
Who for people, which for things, that for both, where for places and whose for possession: The woman whose car is blue lives next door. The shop where I buy rice is near here.

51
00:02:58.383 --> 00:03:01.254
Is the relative pronoun always necessary?

52
00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:13.248
No. When it is the object of the clause we can leave it out: The book I read was long. When it is the subject, we must keep it: The man who called is my uncle.

53
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.842
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.683 --> 00:03:21.620
Grammar focus: Relative clauses: who and which and that and where and whose.

55
00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.188
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.883 --> 00:03:26.521
My teacher is a person who always helps me.

57
00:03:27.417 --> 00:03:29.091
This is the city where I was born.

58
00:03:29.983 --> 00:03:32.470
The woman whose car is blue lives next door.

59
00:03:33.433 --> 00:03:41.357
Use who for people, which for things, that for both, where for places and whose for possession. You can omit the pronoun only if it is the object.

60
00:03:42.117 --> 00:03:45.988
Be careful! Don't say: The man which called is my uncle.

61
00:03:47.933 --> 00:03:50.351
Say: The man who called is my uncle.

62
00:03:50.651 --> 00:03:51.942
Use who for people.

63
00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:55.711
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.698
Who, Which, Where?.

65
00:03:57.998 --> 00:04:00.613
My teacher is a person who always helps me.

66
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.064
The book that I read last week was fascinating.

67
00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:06.892
This is the town where I was born.

68
00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.666
The woman whose car is blue lives next door.

69
00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:14.467
A relative clause connects two ideas smoothly.

70
00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:19.650
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:20.483 --> 00:04:23.226
The man blank lives next door is a doctor.

72
00:04:23.526 --> 00:04:26.576
A, who. B, which. C, where.

73
00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:31.959
The answer is A: who.

74
00:04:33.117 --> 00:04:35.105
This is the school blank I study.

75
00:04:35.405 --> 00:04:38.489
A, who. B, where. C, whose.

76
00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:43.731
The answer is B: where.

77
00:04:44.883 --> 00:04:47.220
The girl blank bag is red is my cousin.

78
00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.069
A, who. B, which. C, whose.

79
00:04:54.633 --> 00:04:56.761
The answer is C: whose.

80
00:04:57.917 --> 00:04:59.591
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:59.891 --> 00:05:05.843
A, The book who I read is long.. B, The book which I read is long.. C, The book where I read is long..

82
00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:12.595
The answer is B: The book which I read is long..

83
00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.329
According to the reading, what do relative clauses connect?

84
00:05:17.629 --> 00:05:22.037
A, two ideas. B, two cities. C, two people.

85
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.948
The answer is A: two ideas.

86
00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:32.529
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:33.383 --> 00:05:35.371
Describe a person you know using 'who'.

88
00:05:44.183 --> 00:05:45.591
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:45.891 --> 00:05:58.031
My cousin is a person who loves music and who plays the guitar very well. He is the boy whose songs make everyone smile. I use who and whose to give more information about him.

90
00:05:58.331 --> 00:06:00.029
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:00.917 --> 00:06:07.354
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and relative clauses: who and which and that and where and whose.

92
00:06:07.654 --> 00:06:13.151
Today's value is appreciation of beauty. Learn to notice and value the beauty around you.

93
00:06:13.451 --> 00:06:15.917
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:16.217 --> 00:06:19.113
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

